WEBVTT

00:00.870 --> 00:04.600
We've learned that the thieves who 
infiltrated Sir Iruma's home last night

00:04.600 --> 00:06.430
were the Divine Light Squadron.

00:06.910 --> 00:08.980
The Divine Light Squadron?

00:09.860 --> 00:14.440
They execute any person they judge as defying
 the teachings of the Church of Divine Light.

00:14.440 --> 00:16.790
They're considered extreme, 
even by other fanatical groups.

00:16.790 --> 00:18.590
The Church of Divine Light?

00:18.590 --> 00:19.970
Meaning...

00:20.380 --> 00:23.080
They were sent by the 
Holy Empire of Sidonia.

00:23.470 --> 00:28.820
Then they weren't there to steal—they 
were after my head from the outset?

00:29.620 --> 00:30.730
That's right.

02:02.220 --> 02:07.230
<b>Episode 9
Resolve</b>

02:02.220 --> 02:07.230
<b>Episode 9
Resolve</b>

02:02.390 --> 02:07.260
It seems the reason for the attack was the 
purification magic device Sir Iruma created.

02:07.510 --> 02:10.220
So it's true, then.

02:10.770 --> 02:14.330
<i>Previously, there was a need 
to regularly use light magic</i>

02:14.330 --> 02:17.960
<i>to purify the settling tanks of 
the sewers beneath the city,</i>

02:17.960 --> 02:22.370
<i>and priests of the Church of Divine Light and
 the Church of Creation took turns doing it.</i>

02:23.410 --> 02:29.200
<i>While the Church of Creation operates on 
donations from believers and didn't charge a fee,</i>

02:29.200 --> 02:35.020
<i>the Church of Divine Light dispatches priests 
from Sidonia and demanded a hefty sum.</i>

02:35.420 --> 02:37.250
To the Church of Divine Light,

02:37.500 --> 02:41.910
you're taking away their
 main source of revenue.

02:41.910 --> 02:46.590
Maybe I should go into hiding 
in another nation for a while.

02:46.590 --> 02:50.190
No, you'll be safer here in Bolton.

02:50.420 --> 02:53.290
Our nation has many believers 
in the Church of Creation,

02:53.290 --> 02:56.510
so we can offer you our proactive support.

02:56.860 --> 02:59.480
I'll increase patrols for the 
knights and the city guard.

02:59.480 --> 03:02.170
We'll also strictly monitor 
who comes and goes from the city.

03:02.420 --> 03:03.250
Good!

03:03.250 --> 03:08.490
In that case, we just need to worry 
about his safety when he's adventurin'.

03:08.690 --> 03:09.460
Huh?!

03:09.460 --> 03:15.520
Wait, given the situation, I was planning to 
refrain from adventurer work for a while....

03:15.520 --> 03:16.590
What're you sayin'?!

03:16.820 --> 03:21.060
Your party is one of the 
top five in the whole town!

03:21.060 --> 03:23.190
Not having you would hurt our guild!

03:23.190 --> 03:25.680
My life's the one in danger here...

03:25.680 --> 03:30.150
I promise to protect you, 
even at the cost of my life.

03:30.150 --> 03:33.110
On top of that, I'm trainin' you, aren't I?

03:33.110 --> 03:37.150
I'll give you the skills to send 'em packin', 
no matter how many times they attack you!

03:37.150 --> 03:38.670
That solves our problems.

03:38.670 --> 03:40.320
<i>Huh?!</i>

03:46.170 --> 03:51.340
<i>What's clear is that Sidonia's 
Church of Divine Light is after me.</i>

03:52.650 --> 03:54.090
<i>Because of me,</i>

03:54.400 --> 03:58.390
<i>Sofia, Maria, and Reyva's lives 
were in danger last night.</i>

04:02.140 --> 04:05.250
Hm, the Wings of Nolyn, huh?

04:05.640 --> 04:11.040
Putting the name of the Goddess in 
your party name is pretty grandiose.

04:11.040 --> 04:12.470
You think it's going too far?

04:13.090 --> 04:14.610
I like it.

04:14.610 --> 04:15.570
Takumi.

04:15.570 --> 04:19.140
It seems like rumors of the attack 
on you have already spread.

04:19.140 --> 04:19.870
Huh?

04:21.750 --> 04:26.560
Along with the exaggerated idea that 
there's a large bounty on your head.

04:27.660 --> 04:28.910
Be careful.

04:28.910 --> 04:30.430
There are some adventurers

04:30.430 --> 04:35.220
who will circumvent the guild and 
accept unscrupulous quests for money.

04:39.520 --> 04:44.400
So you mean there's a strong 
chance we'll be attacked again?

04:44.400 --> 04:45.270
Yeah.

04:45.710 --> 04:48.350
I'm the only one they're after.

04:48.350 --> 04:50.180
I'm really sorry, everyone.

04:50.180 --> 04:52.340
Please stop that, Mr. Takumi!

04:52.340 --> 04:54.740
She's right! You shouldn't 
bow your head to us.

04:54.740 --> 04:58.820
We let our guard down last night, 
but that won't happen again!

04:58.820 --> 05:00.160
I'm ready to go!

05:00.390 --> 05:03.360
I'm here too, so rest assured!

05:03.360 --> 05:06.290
That's bad manners, Maple!

05:06.290 --> 05:07.310
Yes.

05:07.550 --> 05:10.180
I know I have Maple and 
Camellia to help,

05:10.180 --> 05:14.850
but I'd feel bad relying on the knights 
to guard the mansion forever.

05:15.290 --> 05:17.250
So I'm thinking of creating an improved

05:17.250 --> 05:20.050
magical device to erect a 
magical barrier around the mansion.

05:20.670 --> 05:24.950
The idea is to keep out anyone 
who isn't registered with it.

05:25.660 --> 05:28.320
I'll help make that magical device!

05:28.320 --> 05:29.380
I'm counting on it.

05:30.270 --> 05:34.430
That would just leave the times we're 
out handling quests as adventurers.

05:34.430 --> 05:38.390
I think we should promptly look 
for an attacker or a tank.

05:38.980 --> 05:42.130
Barack and Hans both said the same thing.

05:42.360 --> 05:45.810
No men, please!

05:45.810 --> 05:47.010
Roger that.

05:47.010 --> 05:49.080
The problem is where to find such a person.

05:49.430 --> 05:52.790
There are some adventurers who operate solo,

05:52.790 --> 05:56.970
but it would be hard to ask someone to
 quickly forge strong bonds within the party.

05:57.460 --> 06:00.180
I think you should trying 
looking at Mulan's.

06:00.670 --> 06:01.900
True.

06:02.250 --> 06:05.800
Having someone bound by contract 
magic would be safest, huh?

06:05.800 --> 06:08.810
I guess bonds of trust 
 take time to forge.

06:08.810 --> 06:13.380
I-I would trust you even without 
our contract, Mr. Takumi!

06:13.380 --> 06:15.070
The same goes for me!

06:15.450 --> 06:16.950
Sofia?!

06:17.470 --> 06:22.390
My life isn't so cheap that I'd risk 
it for someone I didn't trust.

06:22.390 --> 06:23.730
That's...

06:23.730 --> 06:25.310
so cool!

06:25.310 --> 06:28.060
I wish I had said that.

06:49.000 --> 06:50.870
Alright, let's get started.

06:50.870 --> 06:51.920
Yes!

06:51.920 --> 06:55.230
Is there anything I can do to help?

06:55.530 --> 06:56.690
Sofia?

06:57.730 --> 07:01.140
I wanted to learn more about magical devices.

07:01.470 --> 07:05.330
Considering our future, I want 
to learn more about them, too.

07:06.110 --> 07:07.340
Alright.

07:07.340 --> 07:09.110
Then could you help us?

07:09.330 --> 07:13.950
Could you etch this alchemy circle 
into those metal sheets over there?

07:14.520 --> 07:15.770
Very well.

07:29.870 --> 07:31.190
Mr. Takumi...

07:31.190 --> 07:34.550
You didn't sleep much last night, did you?

07:34.550 --> 07:35.600
Huh?

07:35.600 --> 07:40.330
Oh, no. I was thinking about 
countermeasures for the future.

07:41.520 --> 07:44.310
Onward, Camellia!

07:45.970 --> 07:48.180
That's it! Don't lose to some golem!

07:50.090 --> 07:52.190
That doll's supposed to be a golem?

07:52.440 --> 07:54.910
Camellia, don't let your guard down!

07:54.910 --> 07:57.610
You can't underestimate 
the strength of a golem!

07:58.210 --> 08:02.820
That reminds me, golems fall within 
the realm of alchemy, don't they?

08:02.820 --> 08:03.820
Yeah.

08:04.090 --> 08:08.110
Though the magic circle engraved into 
their control core is far too complex,

08:08.110 --> 08:10.300
so I haven't started trying 
things like that yet.

08:10.550 --> 08:14.780
If we had golems, they'd be 
perfect for attackers or tanks.

08:14.780 --> 08:16.260
Yeah, they would.

08:16.720 --> 08:19.730
My current Mana Manipulation 
skill level isn't high enough, though.

08:19.730 --> 08:23.440
I need a higher level be able to 
control the spell precisely enough.

08:20.350 --> 08:22.660
Go! Go! Go! Go! Go!

08:23.990 --> 08:30.030
I've heard that golems created through alchemy 
are only capable of simple movements.

08:26.980 --> 08:30.170
Go!

08:30.710 --> 08:34.410
Then they wouldn't be useful 
for guarding the mansion.

08:31.650 --> 08:33.760
Faster, faster!

08:34.180 --> 08:35.340
Go! Keep it up!

08:34.410 --> 08:36.920
Okay, let's finish up here.

08:39.820 --> 08:40.860
Good.

08:41.100 --> 08:45.060
The barrier should be erected once 
we install these around the mansion.

08:45.250 --> 08:47.080
<b>Spell Control</b>

08:45.250 --> 08:47.080
<b>Skill</b>

08:45.250 --> 08:47.080
<b>acquired</b>

08:45.250 --> 08:47.080
<b>Skill</b>

08:45.250 --> 08:47.080
<b>has Leveled Up</b>

08:45.250 --> 08:47.080
<b>Mana Manipulation</b>

08:45.970 --> 08:46.700
Oh?

08:47.270 --> 08:48.760
What is it?

08:48.760 --> 08:51.960
Once my Mana Manipulation skill maxed out,

08:51.960 --> 08:55.060
I apparently obtained the 
Spell Control skill.

08:55.290 --> 08:56.870
That's incredible!

08:56.870 --> 09:00.630
I'm sure that's thanks to you completing 
this barrier magical device!

09:00.860 --> 09:03.500
If I level Spell Control, then...

09:03.500 --> 09:06.640
maybe I can attempt to create 
a golem's control core.

09:09.060 --> 09:12.570
<b>Holy Empire of Sidonia</b>

09:09.690 --> 09:12.560
The Divine Light Squadron was captured?

09:12.950 --> 09:15.280
Did they not take their 
own lives on the spot?

09:15.570 --> 09:18.460
We believe they weren't 
given the opportunity to.

09:19.410 --> 09:21.950
Was contract magic used on them?

09:22.150 --> 09:23.220
Most likely.

09:23.220 --> 09:26.250
It has likely already been discovered
that the assault was conducted by

09:26.250 --> 09:28.740
believers from the Church of Divine Light.

09:28.740 --> 09:31.010
This has become troublesome.

09:31.010 --> 09:32.340
Father.

09:32.340 --> 09:36.230
At this point, why don't we put off 
dealing with the Kingdom of Barcula,

09:36.230 --> 09:38.450
and prioritize <i>our</i> plan.

09:39.050 --> 09:41.450
Regarding the magic circle
 we discovered in the ruins...

09:41.450 --> 09:43.310
We failed to analyze it,

09:43.690 --> 09:46.170
but it should be possible 
to activate the summoning

09:46.170 --> 09:48.840
using the explanation written 
in the ancient tomes.

09:48.840 --> 09:51.590
Hm. So, Homer,

09:51.590 --> 09:53.770
when will we be ready to carry that out?

09:54.020 --> 09:57.740
It should two more months, three at the longest,

09:58.090 --> 10:00.940
to gather the mana required.

10:05.830 --> 10:07.030
Phew.

10:07.030 --> 10:09.220
Is it difficult?

10:09.220 --> 10:13.250
I tried on a magic stone, but it 
looks like it won't be that easy.

10:13.250 --> 10:18.070
The golem won't move unless 
we draw the multi-layer magic circle

10:18.070 --> 10:20.470
into the control core.

10:20.470 --> 10:21.380
Yeah.

10:21.380 --> 10:24.970
Master, why do you want a golem so badly?

10:25.310 --> 10:27.930
It'd be reassuring to have one 
guarding our home, right?

10:28.190 --> 10:30.260
But you have me and Camellia.

10:30.260 --> 10:33.560
You have Sofia, Maria, and Reyva, too!

10:33.560 --> 10:38.490
Yeah, but it might be like last time, 
and we won't know how they'll infiltrate.

10:39.360 --> 10:43.350
<i>It looks like I still need to 
raise my Spell Control level.</i>

10:43.950 --> 10:46.920
Hey. Could you tame a golem?

10:46.920 --> 10:47.900
Huh?

10:47.900 --> 10:49.170
<i>Right.</i>

10:49.170 --> 10:51.120
<i>I hadn't thought of that.</i>

10:51.630 --> 10:53.900
<i>Maybe there's a chance!</i>

10:55.020 --> 10:58.530
Well... In the western area 
around the Forest of Death,

10:58.530 --> 11:00.540
there are occasionally stray Stone Golems,

11:00.540 --> 11:03.060
and I've heard that Iron Golems appear

11:03.060 --> 11:06.720
in the ancient dungeon near Horas.

11:06.720 --> 11:08.390
There are dungeons?!

11:08.390 --> 11:10.970
Why, of course...

11:10.970 --> 11:12.720
You didn't know that?

11:12.720 --> 11:17.190
Oh, no, more like I've never 
actually been in one.

11:17.440 --> 11:21.450
Since we have the chance, let's try 
facing an Iron Golem in the dungeon!

11:21.450 --> 11:26.420
Entering a dungeon without a 
tank or attacker would be reckless.

11:26.410 --> 11:29.370
<b>Reckless</b>

11:26.940 --> 11:29.060
R-Right.

11:34.350 --> 11:37.350
<i>Our group headed to the rocky 
plains west of the Forest of Death</i>

11:37.350 --> 11:39.750
<i>where we previously hunted Treants.</i>

11:49.180 --> 11:50.540
It's huge!

11:50.540 --> 11:52.240
It's over three meters tall.

11:52.240 --> 11:53.650
It is.

11:53.990 --> 11:56.200
Finding this golem is a stroke of luck.

11:56.600 --> 11:59.310
It's probably a guardian-class
golem from the ruins.

11:59.570 --> 12:02.570
When trying to defeat it, you aim 
for the magic stone in its chest

12:02.570 --> 12:05.020
and the control core at the center of it.

12:05.540 --> 12:09.320
Destroying the control 
core equals dead golem.

12:09.320 --> 12:12.350
I'd rather not let it die.

12:15.070 --> 12:16.360
Those eyes!

12:16.360 --> 12:18.700
I don't know if they're
weapons or detection devices,

12:18.700 --> 12:20.790
but this might be more 
dangerous than we thought.

12:21.370 --> 12:23.300
Let's pass on that golem.

12:24.480 --> 12:25.500
No.

12:25.500 --> 12:29.350
If it's dangerous, then that means 
it'll be more reliable as an ally.

12:29.590 --> 12:30.700
Mr. Takumi?

12:30.700 --> 12:31.520
Let's go!

12:32.570 --> 12:33.860
Mr. Takumi!

12:33.860 --> 12:35.000
Fan out!

12:35.000 --> 12:36.510
Cover Mr. Takumi!

12:43.940 --> 12:45.010
Mr. Takumi!

12:49.950 --> 12:50.860
Wait!

12:52.420 --> 12:53.490
You mustn't!

12:53.490 --> 12:55.580
It's fine... probably.

12:56.200 --> 13:00.130
It's faint, but I can 
feel a connection between us.

13:00.340 --> 13:02.180
Between you and the golem?

13:05.050 --> 13:06.520
Mr. Takumi!

13:06.780 --> 13:08.860
He's incredibly brave.

13:09.770 --> 13:12.440
<i>I'm actually incredibly scared!</i>

13:12.890 --> 13:17.010
<i>But I don't sense any 
hostility from this golem.</i>

13:18.200 --> 13:19.460
<i>I see.</i>

13:19.460 --> 13:24.580
<i>Was this golem protecting 
ruins related to Lady Nolyn?</i>

13:24.580 --> 13:25.620
<i>In that case...</i>

13:25.610 --> 13:29.580
<b>Blessing</b>

13:25.610 --> 13:29.580
<b>Blessing of Lady Nolyn</b>

13:25.610 --> 13:29.580
<b>Concealed</b>

13:29.770 --> 13:31.930
<i>Is it reacting to Lady Nolyn's blessing?</i>

13:35.080 --> 13:36.500
<b>Guardian Golem</b>

13:35.080 --> 13:36.500
<b>tamed</b>

13:38.060 --> 13:39.970
I managed to tame it.

13:39.970 --> 13:41.340
Huh?!

13:42.200 --> 13:45.440
Then it's our new friend?!

13:45.440 --> 13:47.030
That's right, yeah.

13:47.030 --> 13:48.130
What's its name?!

13:48.780 --> 13:50.060
Its name?

13:55.180 --> 13:56.280
Titan.

13:56.570 --> 13:58.100
Titan?

13:58.100 --> 14:01.470
It's the name of a giant in a myth I know.

13:59.020 --> 14:01.980
<b>Unique Skills</b>

13:59.020 --> 14:01.980
<b>Passive Skills</b>

13:59.020 --> 14:01.980
<b>Active Skills</b>

13:59.020 --> 14:01.980
<b>Regeneration Lv8,
Light of Judgment Lv3</b>

13:59.020 --> 14:01.980
<b>Brute Strength Lv8,
Physical Resistance Lv10,
Magic Resistance Lv5</b>

13:59.020 --> 14:01.980
<b>Martial Arts Lv7,
Clubmanship Lv6,
Sense Presence Lv5,
Sense Magic Lv5,
Earth Magic Lv8</b>

13:59.020 --> 14:01.980
<b>Name</b>

13:59.020 --> 14:01.980
<b>Titan</b>

13:59.020 --> 14:01.980
<b>Takumi Iruma's Pet</b>

13:59.020 --> 14:01.980
<b>m 0 0 l 95 0 95 22 0 22</b>

13:59.020 --> 14:01.980
<b>m 0 0 l 95 0 95 15 0 15</b>

13:59.020 --> 14:01.980
<b>m 0 0 l 95 0 95 9 0 9</b>

13:59.020 --> 14:01.980
<b>Race</b>

13:59.020 --> 14:01.980
<b>Guardian Golem</b>

13:59.020 --> 14:01.980
<b>Age</b>

13:59.020 --> 14:01.980
<b>23,122 Yrs</b>

13:59.020 --> 14:01.980
<b>Level</b>

13:59.020 --> 14:01.980
<b>CND</b>

13:59.020 --> 14:01.980
<b>VIT</b>

13:59.020 --> 14:01.980
<b>m 0 0 l 27 0 27 4 0 4</b>

13:59.020 --> 14:01.980
<b>STA</b>

13:59.020 --> 14:01.980
<b>MANA</b>

13:59.020 --> 14:01.980
<b>DEX</b>

13:59.020 --> 14:01.980
<b>STR</b>

13:59.020 --> 14:01.980
<b>INT</b>

13:59.020 --> 14:01.980
<b>AGI</b>

14:04.440 --> 14:07.150
Titan! Nice to have you!

14:09.870 --> 14:11.910
It looks like it's trying to say something.

14:11.910 --> 14:15.680
It looks like it wants me to 
give it a more versatile body.

14:15.680 --> 14:17.450
Alright. Let's go then.

14:17.450 --> 14:21.320
However, we'll cause a commotion 
if we enter the city like this.

14:21.320 --> 14:23.540
Right. Then I'll use my pocket dimension.

14:27.880 --> 14:29.720
Titan is crumbling!

14:36.700 --> 14:39.040
It's not a giant anymore.

14:39.040 --> 14:40.350
It's cute!

14:40.350 --> 14:44.250
Master! Make it so that Titan can talk to us!

14:44.650 --> 14:47.320
Alright. I'll see what I can do.

14:47.320 --> 14:50.490
<b>The Holy Empire of Sidonia
Several Months After Takumi's Present Time</b>

14:48.400 --> 14:50.780
Come on, come on! What's wrong?!

14:51.200 --> 14:53.170
Finished already, Captain?

14:54.850 --> 14:58.930
Jeez, every last one of you is weak.

14:58.930 --> 15:01.910
Yeah. You don't deserve to be called knights.

15:04.700 --> 15:07.120
Indulging yourselves this early in the day?

15:07.380 --> 15:10.390
Yeah, these girls keep 
begging us for some fun.

15:10.390 --> 15:12.600
It's tough being a popular man.

15:12.600 --> 15:15.210
Have you no shame at all?

15:15.210 --> 15:16.650
What gives, Akane?

15:16.650 --> 15:17.930
Jealous?

15:17.930 --> 15:22.610
It's a little late for that after the 
cold attitude you've been giving us.

15:22.610 --> 15:25.520
Akane, that might be how Akira feels,

15:25.520 --> 15:27.160
but I'll welcome you anytime.

15:28.550 --> 15:30.030
Scumbag.

15:31.670 --> 15:33.820
<i>Titan's new body!</i>

15:34.320 --> 15:37.630
<i>I can go all-out with what 
I want for this, right?!</i>

15:38.030 --> 15:38.960
<i>Of course...</i>

15:38.960 --> 15:41.190
<i>we can't leave out the ability to combine!</i>

15:41.190 --> 15:42.060
There!

15:42.430 --> 15:44.320
I'll synthesize it soon.

15:46.030 --> 15:47.510
<i>Though before that,</i>

15:47.970 --> 15:49.920
<i>I need to settle matters for good.</i>

15:49.920 --> 15:50.680
<i>Right?</i>

15:52.360 --> 15:54.210
People are after my life.

15:54.210 --> 15:57.330
If you remain with me, 
then you'll all be in danger as well.

15:57.330 --> 15:58.690
Like we've said before—

15:59.070 --> 16:01.880
So I'm planning to dissolve our contracts.

16:03.110 --> 16:06.040
You all...  should go your own ways.

16:06.040 --> 16:09.520
I can't place you all in danger as well.

16:09.520 --> 16:10.740
Mr. Takumi!

16:11.010 --> 16:12.540
How long have you been planning this?

16:12.930 --> 16:15.690
Since the day after we were first attacked.

16:15.970 --> 16:18.680
I had sensed something was 
weighing on your mind...

16:19.180 --> 16:20.270
But...

16:21.080 --> 16:22.380
Dissolving our contracts?

16:22.700 --> 16:25.380
I think this is best for everyone.

16:25.380 --> 16:29.210
But then, who's going to 
protect you, Mr. Takumi?!

16:29.380 --> 16:31.820
Fortunately, I managed to tame Titan.

16:32.360 --> 16:34.730
So that's why you did something so reckless?

16:34.730 --> 16:37.590
Maple and Camellia are my pets,

16:37.590 --> 16:39.630
so they'll remain that way, but...

16:40.230 --> 16:43.580
I want the three of you 
to live somewhere safe.

16:43.580 --> 16:44.480
Mr. Takumi!

16:44.750 --> 16:49.000
Of course, I'll pay you a lump sum of 
all the wages you've earned so far

16:49.000 --> 16:50.700
so you can live comfortably.

16:50.950 --> 16:55.330
I'll send your home a 
significant sum as well, Reyva.

16:55.730 --> 16:58.520
That's not what this is about!

16:58.760 --> 17:02.740
Well, I say lump sum, but you 
could call it your severance pay.

17:03.100 --> 17:04.760
I can't consent to this.

17:04.760 --> 17:06.780
I kind of need you to consent to it.

17:08.010 --> 17:09.110
Maria?

17:09.110 --> 17:11.570
If you're intent on dissolving our contracts,

17:12.870 --> 17:15.380
then you'll have to go through me first!

17:15.380 --> 17:16.050
Huh?

17:16.330 --> 17:22.490
Mr. Takumi, why do you always 
prioritize us over yourself?!

17:22.490 --> 17:25.020
Mr. Takumi, you idiot!

17:25.500 --> 17:27.570
Why would you tell us to leave you?!

17:28.550 --> 17:33.860
Because... I don't want to put 
you all in any more danger.

17:34.600 --> 17:38.320
You're all precious to me.

17:38.700 --> 17:40.000
If we're precious,

17:40.000 --> 17:44.510
then why won't you ask us to stay 
with you and fight at your side?!

17:44.910 --> 17:48.870
Why won't you ask us to overcome 
this challenge <i>with</i> you?!

17:49.160 --> 17:52.480
We're the Wings of Nolyn, aren't we?

17:53.010 --> 17:55.430
We're all each other's wings.

17:56.080 --> 17:59.360
You were the one who said that, Mr. Takumi!

17:59.950 --> 18:03.020
If you lose your wings...

18:03.020 --> 18:04.410
then you can't fly anymore.

18:04.760 --> 18:05.800
Maria...

18:08.090 --> 18:09.390
I'm sorry...

18:09.770 --> 18:12.650
for saying such rude things to you!

18:12.980 --> 18:16.320
I'm just... I'm just...

18:22.250 --> 18:23.360
Mr. Takumi,

18:23.650 --> 18:25.900
I know you're concerned about us,

18:26.500 --> 18:28.530
and that's why you're asking us to leave.

18:29.120 --> 18:31.390
I understand that.

18:31.390 --> 18:35.200
So I want you to understand too, Mr. Takumi.

18:36.000 --> 18:38.520
That what you've just said out of concern,

18:39.210 --> 18:44.730
is the cruelest thing you 
could ever say to us.

18:46.380 --> 18:50.740
Master, I'll work hard so that you'll 
keep me for many long years.

18:51.070 --> 18:54.670
I'll work as hard as possible!

18:54.670 --> 18:56.700
I look forward to working with you!

18:56.900 --> 19:02.540
I hereby swear my lifelong 
loyalty to you, Takumi Iruma.

19:03.940 --> 19:04.980
I'm sorry.

19:05.370 --> 19:09.030
I didn't understand how you all truly felt,

19:10.010 --> 19:12.750
and I just pushed my own feelings onto you.

19:13.580 --> 19:14.780
I'm sorry.

19:15.460 --> 19:17.200
I'm still so immature.

19:17.650 --> 19:19.390
I may be immature,

19:19.950 --> 19:23.030
but is it okay to ask you to stay with me?

19:24.110 --> 19:26.500
M-Mr. Takumi!

19:26.810 --> 19:29.760
I've been your bodyguard from the start.

19:29.760 --> 19:31.870
If danger is drawing close,

19:31.870 --> 19:34.490
then all the more reason for 
you to keep me at your side.

19:35.240 --> 19:39.690
My heart and body already 
belong to you, Mr. Takumi.

19:39.940 --> 19:41.800
We live and die together.

19:42.940 --> 19:46.370
My future is with you too, Mr. Takumi.

19:46.590 --> 19:50.320
I don't have another place to go, 
and I don't want one.

19:50.810 --> 19:53.730
I've only just started 
learning things from you,

19:53.730 --> 19:56.300
and I've made up my mind
 to learn more alongside you

19:56.300 --> 19:59.810
and create new things with you!

19:59.810 --> 20:04.830
The Wings of Nolyn really are the best.

